  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an n x n binary matrix grid, it is allowed to change at most one 0 to 1. A group of connected 1s forms an island, where two 1s are connected if they share one of their sides.\n\n\n\nReturn the size of the largest island in the grid after applying this operation.",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= n <= 1000",
      "grid[i][j] is 0 or 1"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "grid = [[1,0], [0,1]]",
    "outputFormat": "The size of the largest island is: 3",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "grid = [[1,0], [0,1]]",
        "output": "3",
        "explanation": "We change one of the 0s to 1, connecting the two existing 1s, which results in an island with a maximum area of 3.\n\n**Example 2:**"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "grid = [[1, 1], [1, 1]]",
        "output": "4",
        "explanation": "The largest island already exists with size 4, as all cells are already connected.\n        \n    \n\n\n**Disclaimer**: Here is the practice link to help you assess your knowledge better. It's highly recommend trying to solve it before looking at the solution."
      }
    ]
  },
